# What a build of the boot environment must not carry into the builder. Every
# `target` is gigabytes of some platform's artefacts — the workspace's, and the
# kernel half's beside it — `.git` is the history, and `.kernel-loop` is the
# supervisor's own state. None of them is compiled, and all of them would be
# copied on every build.
target
**/target
.git
.kernel-loop
